 	Invokes an action on a notification. If _action_ is not specified, invokes
 	the default action. Action names can be discovered using `makoctl list`.
 
+	The application is also sent an xdg-activation token, so it can raise
+	itself the same way it does when the notification is clicked. mako has no
+	input serial of its own at this point -- a D-Bus caller never does -- so it
+	reuses the serial from the last time the pointer entered one of its
+	surfaces, which compositors keep valid for exactly this sort of deferred
+	activation. If the pointer has not touched a notification since mako
+	started there is no such serial, and the action is invoked without a token:
+	it still fires, the window just stays where it is.
+
 	Options:
 
 	*-n* <id>
